\subsection{Checking pointers of the program}

A pointer that a program passes to the kernel is checked before the kernel writes through it, page by page, as the other system
calls do it (\texttt{user\_to\_phys} also copies shared pages and reads back pages that were swapped out).

<<linux_abi.c: user pointers>>=
extern u64 user_to_phys (u64 va, int write);

static int user_ok (u64 va, u64 len, int write) {
  if (len == 0) return 1;
  for (u64 p = va & ~4095UL; p < va + len; p += 4096)
    if (!user_to_phys (p < va ? va : p, write)) return 0;
  return 1;
}

